# GLPI Helpdesk: Installation Guide

> Home lab project. GLPI is the ticketing system for my fictional company SilverBank, running in an Ubuntu container on my Proxmox homelab. Passwords are shown as placeholders and are stored outside this document.

Last updated: 1 November 2026

## Overview

GLPI is an open-source IT service management tool: helpdesk tickets, asset inventory and a knowledge base. I installed it to practise real helpdesk work on my SilverBank lab (Windows Server 2025 Active Directory).

| Item | Value |
| --- | --- |
| Container | Proxmox LXC, CT ID 230, unprivileged |
| Hostname | ln-glpi01 |
| OS | Ubuntu 26.04 LTS |
| IP | 192.168.7.83/24, gateway 192.168.7.1 |
| DNS | 192.168.7.80, 192.168.7.82 (domain controllers), search domain corp.silverbank.internal |
| URL | http://helpdesk.corp.silverbank.internal |
| Resources | 2 vCPU, 2 GB RAM, 20 GB disk |
| Stack | Apache 2.4, PHP 8.5, MariaDB 11.8, GLPI 12.0.1 |

